#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096388 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "210f48cc-8812-564d-9dae-5a8a42165ef9" :question/math-academy-id "e-14005" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ x-\\frac{y}{6} &=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ x-\\frac{y}{6} &=\\frac{5}{2} && |\\,\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =-4 \\\\ x & =-4-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $x=-4-2y$ into the second equation and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-y & =15 \\\\ 6(-4-2y)-y & =15 \\\\ -24-12y-y & =15 \\\\ -24-13y & =15 \\\\ -13y & =39 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation $x=-4-2y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4-2y \\\\  & =-4-2(-3) \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x = 2$ and $y = -3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096389 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "ff844be7-7d1e-5a1f-a4d6-1d4313f5fd2d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14006" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5a+\\frac{3b}{2} &=2 \\\\ \\frac{4a}{3}+2b &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions, we multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5a+\\frac{3b}{2} &=2 && |\\,\\times 2 \\\\ \\frac{4a}{3}+2b &=0 && |\\,\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2,$ then we will get a $-6b$ term that can cancel with the $6b$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10a+3b &=4 && |\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 4a+6b &=0 && \\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $b$-variable, and allows us to solve for $a\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-20a-\\cancel{6b} & =-8 \\\\ 4a+\\cancel{6b} & =0 \\\\ (-20a+4a) & =(-8+0) \\\\ -16a & =-8 \\\\ a & =\\frac{-8}{-16} \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $a=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ into the equation $4a+6b=0$ to solve for $b\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+6b & =0 \\\\ 4(\\frac{1}{2})+6b & =0 \\\\ 2+6b & =0 \\\\ 6b & =-2 \\\\ b & =-\\frac{2}{6} \\\\ b & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a = \\dfrac{1}{2}, \\,b =-\\dfrac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "fb7a4815-45e8-5288-8e96-c3741f1a2097" :question/math-academy-id "e-14732" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x-5y &=-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x+3y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $4.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x-5y &=-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x+3y &=2 && |\\,\\times 4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $-x$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $x$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable, and allows us to solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{x}-5y & =-1 \\\\ \\cancel{x}+12y & =8 \\\\ 7y & =7 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=1$ into the equation $-x-5y=-1$ to solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-5y & =-1 \\\\ -x-5\\cdot 1 & =-1 \\\\ -x-5 & =-1 \\\\ -x & =4 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-4, \\, y=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations Using Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "7f77dc95-b22e-51af-a8c2-ef60ae4f3098" :question/math-academy-id "e-14733" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}x+2y &=3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}x-\\frac{2}{3}y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $6,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}x+2y &=3 && |\\times 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}x-\\frac{2}{3}y &=-7 && |\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $y$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+\\cancel{4y} & =6 \\\\ x-\\cancel{4y} & =-42 \\\\ (5x+x) & =(6-42) \\\\ 6x & =-36 \\\\ x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-6$ into the second equation to solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-4y & =-42 \\\\ -6-4y & =-42 \\\\ -4y & =-36 \\\\ y & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-6$ and $y=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0deee66f-f1c1-5fc7-973a-d2118b0dde4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0deee66f-f1c1-5fc7-973a-d2118b0dde4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288131} :answer-field/id #uuid "666676b7-4b09-5b00-aaa1-e3cae5f5d335" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fef28ec2-8d49-5650-9a07-d4d69ec832b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fef28ec2-8d49-5650-9a07-d4d69ec832b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289721} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fbc86e-8f6d-598c-8e41-15c7fa336d29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4da87082-65b7-55e8-a455-70124fce0262" :question/math-academy-id "q-215738" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+4q &=-6 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{2}+\\frac{5q}{2} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $2.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+4q &=-6 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{2}+\\frac{5q}{2} &=2 && |\\,\\times 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+4q &=-6 \\\\ 3p+5q &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $p$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p+4q & =-6 \\\\ 2p & =-4q-6 \\\\ p & =-2q-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $p=-2q-3$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p+5q & =4 \\\\ 3(-2q-3)+5q & =4 \\\\ -6q-9+5q & =4 \\\\ -q & =13 \\\\ q & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to find the value of $p,$ we substitute $q=-13$ into the equation $p=-2q-3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =-2q-3 \\\\  & =-2(-13)-3 \\\\  & =26-3 \\\\  & =23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=23,\\,q=-13.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e6143a6-0fdd-5669-84d8-0e113cd51643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e6143a6-0fdd-5669-84d8-0e113cd51643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534620} :answer-field/id #uuid "22db2219-dd1d-5c73-8420-03acf31177fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b7dfa22-473e-57b5-a937-ceec1b5ff546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b7dfa22-473e-57b5-a937-ceec1b5ff546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534530} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc1d4df-8587-5128-8fdf-3b45c0f0a1dc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f8f1100-44e9-5de0-ac27-77c13ead7f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-215740" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{1}{3}y=6 \\\\ 5x-y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $3.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{1}{3}y=6 & |\\,\\times 3 \\\\ 5x-y=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+y=18 \\\\ 5x-y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $y$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-y$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable, and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+\\cancel{y} & =18 \\\\ 5x-\\cancel{y} & =4 \\\\ 11x & =22 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=2$ into the equation $6x+y=18$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+y & =18 \\\\ 6\\cdot 2+y & =18 \\\\ 12+y & =18 \\\\ y & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=2,\\,y=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccf4bfc3-88a6-5d09-ae6d-e269ffac1931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccf4bfc3-88a6-5d09-ae6d-e269ffac1931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534724} :answer-field/id #uuid "32fbac1b-2c0d-5963-85ad-5444d6fe7fc9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad656808-65b5-5adb-8dd4-7e9667a6904d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad656808-65b5-5adb-8dd4-7e9667a6904d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534655} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d296c9e-3e4f-5251-b99c-1087847747be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "634cc981-026f-5720-a0d6-757e4b38cffe" :question/math-academy-id "q-215834" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=1 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{y}{9}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $9.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=1 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{y}{9}=-1 & |\\,\\times 9\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=1 \\\\ 6x-y=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $y$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-y & =-9 \\\\ 6x+9 & =y \\\\ y & =6x+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $y=6x+9$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y & =1 \\\\ 5x+2(6x+9) & =1 \\\\ 5x+12x+18 & =1 \\\\ 17x+18 & =1 \\\\ 17x & =-17 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $y,$ we substitute $x=-1$ into the equation $y=6x+9,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6x+9 \\\\  & =6(-1)+9 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1,\\,y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0293fcaf-7265-58db-982d-824c6a56e9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0,\\,y=-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534268} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcca77f-33b4-51d9-b59e-2f22876bcd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534459} {:answer/id #uuid "b1db4db7-8a40-5e37-8cf9-10fa79be6e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\,y=-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534664} {:answer/id #uuid "cd385079-e588-5673-a07b-71dcd96eba0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534725} {:answer/id #uuid "d2977dc8-5522-59a8-9ba9-e7485deb3f09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,\\,y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd385079-e588-5673-a07b-71dcd96eba0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534725} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d9a375-abbc-5813-a298-e638283c175f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98e817d9-610e-538f-a711-341d85a62ad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-216035" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{3}{2}y=-5 \\\\ -2x-y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{3}{2}y=-5 & |\\,\\times 6 \\\\ -2x-y=-2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+9y=-30 \\\\ -2x-y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $2x$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-2x$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable, and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2x}+9y & =-30 \\\\ -\\cancel{2x}-y & =-2 \\\\ 8y & =-32 \\\\ y & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=-4$ into the equation $-2x-y=-2$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-y & =-2 \\\\ -2x-(-4) & =-2 \\\\ -2x+4 & =-2 \\\\ -2x & =-6 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3$ and $y=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b3f5e6-7b2e-56b7-9389-d1e188527eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81b3f5e6-7b2e-56b7-9389-d1e188527eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534547} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cb22693-eb88-5d68-998f-9fb46b5af777" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534858} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "615d06a8-9c96-51de-bff8-a126ddbcc263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "615d06a8-9c96-51de-bff8-a126ddbcc263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534463} :answer-field/id #uuid "b535eccc-73da-535c-a127-32c7c5dd2549" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87b4272d-ed6b-52ae-b49c-9dfe670380e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-216038" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}p-\\frac{1}{4}q=3 \\\\ -4p-7q=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $12.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}p-\\frac{1}{4}q=3 & |\\,\\times 12 \\\\ -4p-7q=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4p-3q=36 \\\\ -4p-7q=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $4p$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-4p$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $p$-variable, and allows us to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{4p}-3q & =36 \\\\ -\\cancel{4p}-7q & =4 \\\\ -10q & =40 \\\\ q & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $q=-4$ into the equation $-4p-7q=4$ to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4p-7q & =4 \\\\ -4p-7\\cdot (-4) & =4 \\\\ -4p+28 & =4 \\\\ -4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $p=6$ and $q=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16636eaa-e2cc-5e82-a93c-29ae2c9a4b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534317} {:answer/id #uuid "590d032f-044c-52af-affe-ade519cfab6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534445} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9268e1-dbb3-5170-96ed-895c49adebf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534613} {:answer/id #uuid "c40a62c3-bbe0-5d17-9e8f-240d7fe1b737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534704} {:answer/id #uuid "efbe8073-8987-54ae-9846-bf0535624288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c9268e1-dbb3-5170-96ed-895c49adebf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534613} :answer-field/id #uuid "172d876b-a2ec-53c9-b98d-a6ec2ea0fdc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f1e5457-cea5-5c5a-997b-b02818578f46" :question/math-academy-id "q-216060" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}a+\\frac{3}{5}b=\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{7}a+\\frac{1}{7}b=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $5$ and the second equation by $7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}a+\\frac{3}{5}b=\\frac{9}{5} & |\\times 5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{7}a+\\frac{1}{7}b=1 & |\\times 7\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5a+3b=9 \\\\ 3a+b=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the second equation can easily be solved for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7-3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $b=7-3a$ into the first equation and then solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a+3b & =9 \\\\ 5a+3(7-3a) & =9 \\\\ 5a+21-9a & =9 \\\\ -4a & =-12 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $b,$ we substitute $a=3$ into the equation $b=7-3a$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7-3a \\\\  & =7-3(3) \\\\  & =7-9 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3$ and $b=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06af144f-4c5a-5f7d-bcae-becd399595a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s=1,\\,t=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534272} {:answer/id #uuid "35184dd6-b1fe-5c13-bdb5-273a2cadca99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s=3,\\,t=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534366} {:answer/id #uuid "80d413a7-4a8a-5e3d-8f60-ce6ec9e391fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s=2,\\,t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534543} {:answer/id #uuid "90a54c3b-d57a-5b56-b610-4e5ba4b8c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s=0,\\,t=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534586} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f2c462-fa61-5493-90fc-306d1d3339be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s=-1,\\,t=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06af144f-4c5a-5f7d-bcae-becd399595a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s=1,\\,t=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534272} :answer-field/id #uuid "86ae1002-c318-5989-8c0c-03e862059522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb34e92b-11ce-5586-a6db-ed20acf39bd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-216062" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}s-\\frac{2}{3}t=-1 \\\\ s+\\frac{1}{4}t=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}s-\\frac{2}{3}t=-1 & |\\times 3 \\\\ s+\\frac{1}{4}t=2 & |\\times 4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5s-2t=-3 \\\\ 4s+t=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the second equation can easily be solved for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4s+t & =8 \\\\ t & =8-4s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $t=8-4s$ into the first equation and then solve for $s:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5s-2t & =-3 \\\\ 5s-2(8-4s) & =-3 \\\\ 5s-16+8s & =-3 \\\\ 13s & =13 \\\\ s & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $t,$ we substitute $s=1$ into the equation $t=8-4s$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =8-4s \\\\  & =8-4(1) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $s=1$ and $t=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53744223-8cd7-552e-a59b-eb16d6ea99ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8,\\,y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534430} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ccee43-d730-5189-89d6-32f56294f8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8,\\,y=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534677} {:answer/id #uuid "d224f1c2-daea-5840-bde5-ea7d182fed3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534735} {:answer/id #uuid "d6375d72-3485-5e65-848c-9b62e50dff15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=12,\\,y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534749} {:answer/id #uuid "fa92e62f-e86c-521d-82dc-8c0da4ab37e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53744223-8cd7-552e-a59b-eb16d6ea99ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8,\\,y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534430} :answer-field/id #uuid "49233c73-c921-5e3f-b3db-c183bb683e95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecc873f4-57df-56ae-b5fa-d73b11c36cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-216177" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}x+2y=-6 \\\\ -x+\\frac{1}{3}y=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}x+2y=-6 & |\\times 4 \\\\ -x+\\frac{1}{3}y=-10 & |\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+8y=-24 \\\\ -3x+y=-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $x$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3x}+8y & =-24 \\\\ -\\cancel{3x}+y & =-30 \\\\ (8y+y) & =(-24-30) \\\\ 9y & =-54 \\\\ y & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=-6$ into the first equation to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+8y & =-24 \\\\ 3x+8(-6) & =-24 \\\\ 3x-48 & =-24 \\\\ 3x & =24 \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=8,\\,y=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05248fe5-5f7a-5b88-bac4-277d935e8d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=6,\\,b=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288068} {:answer/id #uuid "40732601-d1fe-5462-bcbf-5ac0de185f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288473} {:answer/id #uuid "5d759700-7377-5b33-a932-dd76dd087e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-8,\\,b=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288684} {:answer/id #uuid "860b4286-7355-5ef0-8cf0-49399f52b04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=8,\\,b=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288939} {:answer/id #uuid "e616263a-88d6-5509-9955-bcea3d00e6d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d759700-7377-5b33-a932-dd76dd087e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-8,\\,b=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288684} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b7b004d-1ebf-54fc-bed6-9e2d986b4568" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2738428-0a2a-5ef8-946f-188443bb06da" :question/math-academy-id "q-216309" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}a+b &=-3 \\\\ a-\\frac{1}{3}b &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}a+b &=-3 && |\\times 4 \\\\ a-\\frac{1}{3}b &=-9 && |\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3a+4b &=-12 \\\\ 3a-b &=-27\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-3a$ term that can cancel with the $3a$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3a+4b &=-12 && |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 3a-b &=-27 && \\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3a-4b &=12 \\\\ 3a-b &=-27\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $a$-variable, and allows us to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{3a}-4b & =12 \\\\ \\cancel{3a}-b & =-27 \\\\ (-4b-b) & =(12-27) \\\\ -5b & =-15 \\\\ b & =\\frac{-15}{-5} \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $b=3$ into the second equation to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-b & =-27 \\\\ 3a-3 & =-27 \\\\ 3a & =-24 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{24}{3} \\\\ a & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $a=-8,\\,b=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a013722-8f9f-5321-aba5-d0f35846b7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=5,\\,q=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534282} {:answer/id #uuid "15dcd2e7-aa75-5856-821e-3902315292cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-5,\\,q=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534315} {:answer/id #uuid "393fa023-30ea-53d4-bbe5-359af3c3e54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=4,\\,q=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534374} {:answer/id #uuid "53c886c8-25e2-5dd5-886f-89fc9f4a4c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1,\\,q=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534432} {:answer/id #uuid "b5179a50-ba34-5521-9234-e0c0ccc5947f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=3,\\,q=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15dcd2e7-aa75-5856-821e-3902315292cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-5,\\,q=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534315} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ba83247-057c-59a6-9333-3de8fa7c2437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "075ffa39-e6dc-5458-b079-fafe8364cbd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-52198" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}p+q=1 \\\\ -2p-3q=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $5.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}p+q=1 & |\\,\\times 5 \\\\ -2p-3q=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+5q=5 \\\\ -2p-3q=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $2p$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-2p$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $p$-variable, and allows us to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2p}+5q & =5 \\\\ -\\cancel{2p}-3q & =1 \\\\ 2q & =6 \\\\ q & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $q=3$ into the equation $2p+5q=5$ to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p+5q & =5 \\\\ 2p+5\\cdot 3 & =5 \\\\ 2p+15 & =5 \\\\ 2p & =-10 \\\\ p & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-5$ and $q=3.$"}]}
